WEBVTT

00:26.270 --> 00:27.360
Endorsi?

00:27.360 --> 00:31.670
Should you have ditched your 
beloved Rachel to come here?

00:33.960 --> 00:35.680
You're such a romantic.

00:36.340 --> 00:40.180
Where I'm from, we didn't 
have flowers or the moon.

00:40.610 --> 00:45.190
Huh. Lucky Rachel. She gets all the attention.

00:45.830 --> 00:48.470
I'd like a reward, too.

00:48.470 --> 00:49.760
A reward?

00:49.760 --> 00:52.560
For being strong and useful.

00:52.560 --> 00:55.200
I think I work pretty hard.

00:55.820 --> 00:58.450
What would you like as a reward?

00:58.730 --> 01:02.040
Well, let's see... Maybe a date?

01:02.510 --> 01:03.950
What's a date?

01:04.280 --> 01:12.450
It's when you spend a whole day doing 
everything you can to make me happy

01:12.450 --> 01:15.160
and think only of me.

01:15.900 --> 01:17.390
Very well.

01:17.390 --> 01:18.970
What? Really?

01:19.380 --> 01:25.980
I'm not sure if I can do this "date" thing 
correctly, but if we pass the test...

01:26.260 --> 01:29.230
I'm looking forward to 
being rewarded with a date.

01:33.130 --> 01:34.490
Are you all right?

01:35.260 --> 01:36.410
Thanks.

01:36.740 --> 01:37.490
Um...

01:38.250 --> 01:42.240
Maybe I should mind my own business, but 
perhaps you should wear different shoes.

01:44.030 --> 01:48.000
I guess no one will notice if I step 
outside my display case a little.

01:48.000 --> 01:49.040
Huh?

01:49.040 --> 01:52.330
So what kind of shoes do 
you think would suit me?

01:53.360 --> 01:56.130
I don't know much about fashion.

01:57.020 --> 01:59.230
But I think you should wear 
shoes that are easy to move in.

02:09.540 --> 02:10.480
<i>Endorsi?</i>

02:10.480 --> 02:13.480
What is this hunk of metal?

02:24.930 --> 02:27.000
We finally meet...

02:28.050 --> 02:30.190
Jue Viole Grace.

04:01.010 --> 04:05.010
<b>Episode 15</b>

04:01.010 --> 04:05.010
<b>The Promise of That Day</b>

04:10.690 --> 04:12.110
Damn it!

04:12.110 --> 04:14.410
<i>Is this really the only way?!</i>

04:14.790 --> 04:16.400
Just trust me.

04:16.400 --> 04:20.400
Like hell! I don't believe a word you say!

04:20.880 --> 04:24.030
You don't want to wait for all 
your teammates to die, do you?

04:24.940 --> 04:26.180
<i>Then run.</i>

04:27.960 --> 04:30.410
Jue Viole Grace?

04:30.410 --> 04:35.190
I heard you were a jacked long-haired 
guy, but you're a skinny little thing.

04:37.820 --> 04:39.420
Why don't you say something?

04:39.420 --> 04:41.300
Raise your head.

04:41.570 --> 04:46.050
U-Um, there must be some mistake.

04:50.870 --> 04:54.690
Th-This person isn't a FUG 
member or anything like that.

04:57.930 --> 04:59.140
He's...

05:04.260 --> 05:05.360
<i>I'm frozen?</i>

05:22.580 --> 05:24.260
Do you have any spare bombs?

05:24.720 --> 05:28.140
Yes, but they're anti-tank explosives.

05:29.150 --> 05:30.520
I'll kill you!

05:31.800 --> 05:33.570
Throw them all! Hurry!

05:33.570 --> 05:34.520
But...

05:35.520 --> 05:36.560
Hurry!

05:45.520 --> 05:48.780
Who throws anti-tank explosives 
at a delicate lady?

05:52.790 --> 05:54.700
I'll kill them once I find them.

05:54.700 --> 05:57.580
No, I'll torture them to death!

05:59.170 --> 06:00.920
<i>But that ability just now...</i>

06:11.170 --> 06:13.840
I'm in a bad mood here.

06:16.870 --> 06:20.390
I never thought I'd get to 
see Endorsi Jahad in person.

06:21.180 --> 06:25.440
She's cute, but she's terrifying. 
Still cute, though.

06:26.520 --> 06:28.970
Surely she's given up the pursuit.

06:29.560 --> 06:30.990
I hope you're right.

06:31.570 --> 06:34.650
Anyway, what happened 
to you is terrible, Bam.

06:35.150 --> 06:37.950
How could she mistake you 
for Jue Viole Grace?

06:38.850 --> 06:42.000
There's no way you're a bad guy like him.

06:42.980 --> 06:45.540
The patrols have stopped chasing us.

06:46.890 --> 06:49.150
It sounds like something 
has started up above.

06:49.150 --> 06:51.560
We should probably part ways here.

06:52.150 --> 06:53.260
Right.

06:53.730 --> 06:55.970
I'm glad I met you, Bam.

06:59.340 --> 07:00.830
See you on the <i>Archimedes</i>.

07:10.360 --> 07:14.580
The grand prize of this Workshop 
Battle is a human being.

07:17.880 --> 07:19.280
<i>What's going on?</i>

07:21.540 --> 07:24.170
<i>In any case, I need to get back.</i>

07:27.810 --> 07:33.130
Burning guys who were too afraid 
to shoot is so much fun!

07:34.630 --> 07:37.140
I like this game.

07:37.140 --> 07:39.640
So, who should I burn next?

07:39.930 --> 07:42.530
Slow down, Quaetro.

07:49.610 --> 07:52.860
Let's head somewhere up high next.

07:52.860 --> 07:56.170
Really? I love heights!

07:57.260 --> 07:59.560
Things have calmed down below.

07:59.980 --> 08:01.870
Yeah. It's awfully quiet.

08:02.260 --> 08:04.950
We can't keep hiding forever.

08:05.810 --> 08:07.380
Let's go.

08:08.210 --> 08:09.510
You're right.

08:09.510 --> 08:12.630
We're screwed if we can't 
get onto the <i>Archimedes</i>.

08:13.320 --> 08:15.640
Follow us and be careful.

08:17.000 --> 08:18.260
O-Okay.

08:21.170 --> 08:22.270
Well, well.

08:25.310 --> 08:27.230
Chang Blarode.

08:27.800 --> 08:29.920
We didn't have to go far to find you.

08:30.240 --> 08:32.610
Were you that desperate to see me?

08:34.110 --> 08:34.950
Too slow!

08:38.100 --> 08:42.040
You just have to hit me. 
There's no need to aim for the head.

08:42.460 --> 08:45.370
Drop the gun. Don't bother trying to resist.

08:45.370 --> 08:47.460
Right back at you!

08:50.170 --> 08:52.420
Y-Yoo-hoo.

08:52.870 --> 08:56.550
If you want to keep him 
in the game, drop the gun.

08:57.890 --> 08:59.580
Quaetro.

09:00.830 --> 09:03.380
How'd you get here?

09:04.360 --> 09:06.050
Can't you tell?

09:07.780 --> 09:09.570
He ran here.

09:10.880 --> 09:13.080
So the people who haven't passed yet

09:13.080 --> 09:17.520
are either cowards too scared 
to shoot a gun or after an item.

09:18.450 --> 09:23.450
I figured we wouldn't get shot even 
if we brazenly ran up right now.

09:24.010 --> 09:26.460
By the way, I came here by Lighthouse.

09:26.710 --> 09:27.590
What?

09:27.590 --> 09:31.340
I'm using my head to come 
up with a plan here.

09:31.340 --> 09:33.410
I don't have energy to waste.

09:33.410 --> 09:35.380
Dude, screw you!

09:35.380 --> 09:36.470
It's all good.

09:36.470 --> 09:40.760
We were able to save them because 
you decided to start running.

09:40.760 --> 09:42.490
I'd hardly call that good!

09:42.940 --> 09:45.390
I heard you died.

09:45.390 --> 09:46.070
Huh?

09:50.970 --> 09:52.900
Long time no see.

09:52.900 --> 09:56.780
Why are you hanging around with this trash?

09:56.780 --> 09:58.080
Trash?

09:58.080 --> 10:00.410
Can I burn this guy?

10:00.410 --> 10:03.390
Don't create more problems for me.

10:03.390 --> 10:05.320
It's complicated.

10:05.830 --> 10:07.530
You guys are lucky.

10:07.530 --> 10:08.920
How?!

10:08.920 --> 10:11.010
Normally, if you ended up in this situation,

10:11.010 --> 10:14.290
you'd both be shot and 
taken out of the game.

10:14.290 --> 10:15.060
Huh?!

10:17.280 --> 10:19.050
Be direct.

10:19.340 --> 10:22.370
Let's make a deal. I'll let you choose.

10:22.370 --> 10:26.120
Will you drop out of the game, 
or will you give us all your bullets?

10:26.120 --> 10:27.180
What?!

10:27.180 --> 10:28.640
I'm not finished.

10:29.060 --> 10:33.800
If you give us all your bullets, we'll send 
you to the Archimedes using light shots.

10:33.800 --> 10:34.440
Oh?

10:34.440 --> 10:36.510
Not a bad deal, right?

10:37.110 --> 10:39.450
What if I don't like either choice?

10:39.760 --> 10:42.190
I know how strong you two are.

10:42.520 --> 10:48.580
Despite your massive disadvantage, 
you'd still kill a few people fighting back.

10:49.830 --> 10:53.010
But you know, don't you?

10:53.520 --> 10:57.960
You have no chance of beating 
me by fighting me here.

10:59.290 --> 11:03.170
If you don't understand, 
then ask that right eye of yours.

11:05.090 --> 11:06.920
You don't play fair.

11:16.620 --> 11:18.760
Khun, thanks for coming.

11:18.760 --> 11:21.030
Now let's find Miseng and Prince.

11:21.030 --> 11:23.340
We're ignoring them for now.

11:23.340 --> 11:24.020
Huh?

11:24.020 --> 11:28.120
We can't afford to look for people 
we can't get in touch with.

11:28.340 --> 11:29.120
But...

11:29.430 --> 11:32.420
Let's get out of this game while we can.

11:32.420 --> 11:33.880
B-But...

11:33.880 --> 11:37.380
What if they're in danger?

11:37.380 --> 11:40.340
Then they should do something 
about it themselves.

11:40.340 --> 11:44.890
How are we supposed to win the Workshop 
Battle with teammates who can't do that?

11:46.690 --> 11:50.580
A team of people who can't solve their 
own problems and put others in danger

11:50.930 --> 11:53.150
can hardly be called a team.

11:53.720 --> 11:57.020
Well, no, but...

11:57.020 --> 12:00.400
Trust them and get out of the game first.

12:00.740 --> 12:03.490
That's how we can help each other.

12:04.030 --> 12:05.030
Am I wrong?

12:05.940 --> 12:07.950
You can't expect us to 
have an answer to that.

12:07.950 --> 12:09.770
Khun is right.

12:11.180 --> 12:15.040
Let's trust them and get out ourselves.

12:16.370 --> 12:17.040
Shoot me.

12:17.800 --> 12:21.430
A wise decision. In that case...

12:22.830 --> 12:24.360
See you on the ship.

12:53.290 --> 12:56.460
You got a lot of bullets, Verdi.

12:56.460 --> 12:57.640
Yeah.

12:57.640 --> 13:00.210
By the way, who are they?

13:03.560 --> 13:06.140
I like them, so I'm keeping them.

13:06.140 --> 13:08.050
I'm gonna make them my puppets.

13:10.930 --> 13:13.930
They're cute. I want them to get married.

13:13.930 --> 13:16.780
There you go again.

13:16.780 --> 13:19.940
Let's go. The princess will 
be angry if we're late again.

13:20.580 --> 13:21.690
Okay.

13:23.490 --> 13:24.690
Leader.

13:24.930 --> 13:27.680
<i>Including Verdi, we've all met up.</i>

13:27.680 --> 13:30.830
<i>We're currently waiting in 
our designated positions.</i>

13:30.830 --> 13:32.830
Nice work.

13:36.440 --> 13:41.340
It's time. Let's get this show on the road.

13:41.850 --> 13:43.210
All positions, get ready.

13:46.790 --> 13:49.380
<i>As planned, we'll begin 
our attack with a spear.</i>

13:54.820 --> 13:57.300
<i>We're going to enter their hotel.</i>

14:04.580 --> 14:05.830
Reflejo.

14:09.060 --> 14:11.650
Has Viole returned?

14:12.160 --> 14:13.740
The enemy Spear Bearer is on the move.

14:16.110 --> 14:19.160
<i>They're probably jamming 
the inside of the building,</i>

14:19.160 --> 14:20.750
<i>so you'll have to use your own judgment.</i>

14:22.530 --> 14:24.750
<i>Our objectives are total 
annihilation of the enemy...</i>

14:25.690 --> 14:29.260
and to capture Jue Viole Grace alive.

14:32.770 --> 14:34.420
<i>Let's show them...</i>

14:42.370 --> 14:45.850
<i>who controls the E-Rank Regular area.</i>

14:47.880 --> 14:49.150
I've got this.

14:51.580 --> 14:54.050
That was quite the flashy entrance.

14:55.580 --> 14:57.840
Are you here to get revenge for them?

14:57.840 --> 14:59.650
Then turn around and leave.

15:00.020 --> 15:01.920
There's no point in fighting.

15:04.460 --> 15:08.920
But lizards don't seem 
very interested in that.

15:09.220 --> 15:10.450
What?

15:18.070 --> 15:19.920
I wasn't expecting to find you here.

15:20.620 --> 15:23.440
It's been a while, Devil of the Right Arm.

15:24.480 --> 15:28.690
The enemy Spear Bearer has entered 
through the second floor hallway.

15:28.690 --> 15:32.070
Cassano is engaged in combat 
with another enemy outside.

15:33.020 --> 15:36.910
<i>So far, those are the only two 
we've been able to confirm.</i>

15:36.910 --> 15:38.700
Have you heard from Viole?

15:39.600 --> 15:40.510
<i>Not yet.</i>

15:41.090 --> 15:42.210
Then we have no choice.

15:42.810 --> 15:46.470
<i>For now, remain in your positions 
and keep your ears open.</i>

15:46.470 --> 15:48.290
<i>Xia Xia, can you hear me?</i>

15:48.290 --> 15:49.340
You're late!

15:49.660 --> 15:51.560
<i>Where have you been?</i>

15:51.560 --> 15:54.090
<i>You suddenly went missing, and no 
one could get in touch with you!</i>

15:54.090 --> 15:56.400
I'm sorry! I'll be back soon!

15:56.400 --> 15:57.350
<i>Well, hurry up!</i>

15:57.860 --> 16:01.280
<i>We have a situation here! 
Enemies showed up at the hotel!</i>

16:01.280 --> 16:02.170
Enemies?

16:02.700 --> 16:05.360
<i>Anaak Jahad and her friends!</i>

16:05.910 --> 16:07.250
You fool!

16:11.250 --> 16:14.490
You must be insane to cross this area alone!

16:23.000 --> 16:24.920
Hold still!

16:25.870 --> 16:26.920
No, thanks.

16:31.760 --> 16:35.700
Seriously? I thought you 
came to stop the fight.

16:35.700 --> 16:37.800
There's no talking to a lizard.

16:41.070 --> 16:44.440
You'll regret blocking that 
instead of dodging it.

16:44.440 --> 16:45.190
Huh?

16:52.280 --> 16:53.970
Are you worried about your teammates?

16:54.470 --> 16:57.450
What is the Devil of the 
Right Arm doing with FUG?

16:57.900 --> 16:59.880
What's your relationship with FUG?

17:03.740 --> 17:04.910
What do you think you're doing?

17:05.610 --> 17:10.550
I'm not interested in a 
sloppy shootout with you.

17:14.650 --> 17:17.500
Did you learn nothing from your defeat?

17:22.730 --> 17:25.550
You can't land a single blow on me.

17:25.880 --> 17:26.940
Don't underestimate me.

17:27.320 --> 17:29.010
I'm not.

17:29.440 --> 17:34.380
I'm saying you can't defeat an Ignition 
Weapon like me with that sword.

17:39.930 --> 17:44.970
Damn. I didn't think we'd run into the 
Devil of the Right Arm again here.

17:44.970 --> 17:47.210
Are we doomed to have terrible luck?

17:47.210 --> 17:49.930
Was it all right to let him go alone?

17:49.930 --> 17:53.460
I heard Hatz lost to him once before.

17:54.080 --> 17:58.470
Yeah. He ended up dueling 
him on the 20th floor...

17:59.560 --> 18:01.390
and suffered a crushing defeat.

18:02.580 --> 18:06.500
We managed to pass the test 
thanks to the efforts of others,

18:06.500 --> 18:09.480
but Hatz took it pretty hard.

18:09.840 --> 18:12.360
And yet he sought out a fight with him?

18:12.360 --> 18:14.610
Maybe he found a way to beat him.

18:14.970 --> 18:18.340
There's nothing like that. Don't worry.

18:18.340 --> 18:19.990
When it comes to revenge,

18:20.480 --> 18:23.990
whoever's more desperate tends to win.

18:24.910 --> 18:27.250
Is that all you have to say?

18:29.160 --> 18:33.000
Then why not worry about your own arm next?

18:41.770 --> 18:42.890
Come.

18:52.930 --> 18:56.030
What changed? Is it your weapon?

18:56.350 --> 18:58.120
Nothing changed.

18:58.580 --> 19:01.030
I just started practicing twice as much.

19:01.030 --> 19:02.130
That's absurd.

19:03.020 --> 19:06.040
In that case, I'll kill him 
before I consume him.

19:13.840 --> 19:15.170
I must thank you.

19:15.570 --> 19:20.010
After that defeat, I swung 
my sword millions of times

19:20.690 --> 19:23.830
and became a stronger and 
sharper sword than you.

19:27.220 --> 19:29.020
Are you stupid?

19:29.590 --> 19:34.590
She may only be a half-breed, but you
 underestimated someone with Jahad blood.

19:37.530 --> 19:39.170
What a pain.

19:46.340 --> 19:47.730
I'll ask you again.

19:48.280 --> 19:50.210
Why are you with FUG?

19:50.490 --> 19:52.980
You're the ultimate weapon.

19:53.290 --> 19:56.710
What are you trying to gain 
from the Workshop Battle?

19:58.280 --> 20:01.000
A sword that becomes stronger 
with its wielder, huh?

20:01.910 --> 20:03.120
I'm jealous.

20:08.740 --> 20:10.020
Something's coming?

20:24.720 --> 20:26.170
Sorry, swordsman.

20:27.460 --> 20:29.290
See you at the Workshop Battle.

20:31.270 --> 20:33.260
What are those? Clouds?

20:37.680 --> 20:40.090
Is he trying to obscure my vision?

20:42.130 --> 20:43.510
This is pointless.

20:48.020 --> 20:49.010
There you are!

20:51.300 --> 20:53.350
Wrong.

20:57.440 --> 20:58.520
Why, you...

21:01.280 --> 21:02.990
You're so noisy.

21:05.610 --> 21:06.410
Damn it!

21:11.710 --> 21:12.540
Blood?

21:15.040 --> 21:16.770
<i>What's his deal?</i>

21:16.770 --> 21:19.040
<i>He hasn't lost his composure 
even though I hit him.</i>

21:21.660 --> 21:23.300
I don't like it.

21:36.380 --> 21:39.900
Is that where you're hiding?!

21:42.440 --> 21:44.220
Wrong again.

21:47.070 --> 21:49.620
<i>Was this his goal from the start?!</i>

21:51.840 --> 21:53.700
Gotcha, lizard.

21:53.920 --> 21:57.790
Who caught who, now?!

22:04.050 --> 22:05.840
Please stop!

23:46.530 --> 23:49.080
Who throws anti-tank explosives 
at a delicate lady?!

23:49.080 --> 23:51.030
I was right!

23:49.090 --> 23:51.250
<b>Next Time
The 25th Bam</b>
